**Key Accountabilities**
* Build SJ/SMEC’s reputation as a leading consultant with a strong reputation for innovation, technical excellence, quality and project delivery;
* Provide technical risk (and opportunity) governance to both proposals and projects to achieve reliable project performance in terms of sophistication, timeliness and quality (e.g. as Proposal/Project Director);
* Support management to provide technical leadership to employees to ensure cohesion, optimal performance, resourcing, retention and professional development of technical staff;
* Support management to achieve sustainable growth of the business through targeted client relationship management (CRM) and business development (BD) activity.


**Experience**
 Atleast 20\+ years of Professional Industry Experience




* Established international industry profile, recognised as a leader in Ports and Maritime;
* Sought out at industry forums.


**Has The Demonstrated Ability To Consistently**
* Provide key technical expertise across a broad range of high profile projects;
* Manage risk on substantial projects;
* Apply safety in design practices and processes;
* Deliver best client outcomes which have resulted in cost savings;
* Establish and maintain client relationships;
* Bring in new business through business development activities;
* Building technical capability of others;
* Provide expert advice and undertake key high level and complex technical tasks with a high degree of independence across a broad range of medium to large projects;
* Successfully monitor and manage the scope and risk of multiple complex and varying size projects and apply business systems;
* Prepare high level complex technical reports and prepare successful proposals on medium to large projects;
* Utilise excellent time management skills with the ability to efficiently plan workloads and meet deadlines;
* Effectively work across a variety of projects continuously learning and applying new skills and knowledge quickly and efficiently;
* Effectively manage client relationships and expectations
* Provide leadership, supervision and coaching to other staff;
* Effectively engage key stakeholders to result in superior project outcomes which meet or exceed client expectations.


**Skills/Knowledge**
* Demonstrated leadership ability;
* High level technical knowledge;
* Business planning, budgeting and commercial acumen;
* High level consulting and client management skills;
* 
* Proven high level project management skills;
* An understanding of the business / organisation / marketing context of business solutions;
* High level of client service orientation;
* Good national and international industry awareness and market knowledge;
* Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively within a diverse and multi\-disciplinary environment;
* Skilled in managing a co\-operative and flexible work style to work in a team environment;
* Ability to source and apply new knowledge including industry information and key talent;
* Highly skilled in managing competing priorities and working under pressure;
* Computer literacy with proficiency in a variety of relevant computer programs;
* Sound understanding of SMEC's organisational capability and how to access it;
* Aware of SMEC Business Systems in particular:
* Project Management
* WHS Management
* High level application of CRM principals.


 At Surbana Jurong, we put talent, hard work, teamwork and a fun workplace together to approach problems and solve them creatively and collaboratively. Join us in making a positive impact on the world!

The role is responsible for discharging Project Management activities across the Qatar In\-Service Typhoon Availability Service Operation at Dukhan Airbase, Qatar, as CAM133\. This role will undertake Project Management activities within the respective technical delivery areas to ensure key PM tenets are discharged and upheld.




 The incumbent will be required to gather, synthesize \& integrate information relating to performance (cost, resources and outputs), generate, monitor and report progress against plans, identify trends, analyze and interpret data and information to ensure all data and information is accurate, generate and publish regular reports, including internal contract review packs and external customer facing material




 This role will be geographically deployed out into the respective delivery area, providing a Project Management service into the allocated area. Hierarchically, this role will report into the Project Management Lead, who will provide support, leadership and the PM governance framework the incumbent will be required to operate within.




 The role will also be required to support and conduct any ad\-hoc PM activities required due to the nature of Operations at Dukhan Airbase.




**Project Management**
* Provide deployed Project Management support to Dukhan Delivery areas
* Run a subset of the Dukhan Business Rhythm within each delivery area, ensuring Risk, Opportunity, Change (Organisational or Technical) and Spend are reviewed within each team
* Co\-ordinate, facilitate and compile agreed OPR inputs on behalf of each delivery area
* Act as the deployed Project Management conscience of the Dukhan Operation, ensuring delivery areas remain within governance, escalating issues as required.
* Operate as ‘critical friends’ of the deployed areas, providing a valued Project Management service whilst driving and upholding PM values and standards
* Support compilation of PM\&C artefacts into the drumbeat Dukhan SMT Business Rhythm reviews (for example, Change Requests)
* Champion Continuous Improvement initiatives into the CI lead, seeking to maximise operational efficiency and minimising costs;
* Responsible for managing the financial information for the allocated area, to feed the Contract Status Reports (CSR);
* Responsible for managing the Risk and Opportunities (financial, quality, scope and quality) within the allocated area
* Develop, manage and maintain integrated program schedules for non\-recurring elements of wor
* Manage and measure delivery against the contract, advising on contractual compliance / shortfalls for both BAES and the QEAF (BFP/R)
* Co\-ordinate, control and report against internal and contractual KPI’s
* Act as an interface with junior officers within the QEAF for the allocated area for all applicable Project Delivery requirements
* Responsible for managing the resource manpower within the allocated area from a PM standpoint (e.g. cost, resource planning, capacity modelling)
* Support reviews (preparation or attendance) including but not limited to OPR, QCRs, QBRs, risk \& opportunity, Change Control Boards, Business Operations and customer PRMs;
* Provide support to the Business Management Lead for control of the Resource management aspects of the Typhoon Availability Service


**Additional Responsibilities / Activities**
* Ensure compliance with the mandated BAE Systems Governance Framework, including, but not limited to; Life Cycle Management (LCM), Business Continuity Management (BCM) – Incident Management (IM), Gifts \& Hospitality (G\&H), Responsible Document Record Management (RDRM), Export Control, SHE, et al.
* This role will also be required to support and conduct any ad\-hoc PM activities required due to the nature of Operations at Dukhan Airbase.


**Requirements**
**Qualifications/Functional Knowledge:**
**Functional Knowledge \& Experience**
* Experienced and in\-depth Project Control knowledge and techniques in an Operational Aircraft Support environment is preferred;
* Experienced resource demand management and forecasting;
* High level of MS Office knowledge and application;
* Programme Reporting experience;
* Understanding and appreciation of operating in a customer\-focused organisation in the Middle East;
* Commercial and Contractual Awareness;
* Purchasing Process and Export control awareness;
* Contract Status Reporting (CSRs).


**Business Expertise**
* Requires good analytical skills, able to manipulate data to identify trends and data shortages. At this level is able to assess if data is complete, accurate and turn into management information for onwards reporting
* Requires the ability to appropriately engage with and challenge a wide range of stakeholders on project performance
* Understands and is able to use and interpret all project management tools sets.
* Requires a good understanding of the work breakdown structure for the service area or project
* Capable of performing detailed performance analysis using a range of PM toolsets and techniques


**Aspirational Experience Of Using The Following Systems**
* JIRA
* Confluence / Tableau


**Qualifications**
* L6 Project Management Degree (complete or in\-progress), or an extensive amount of practical knowledge gained through experience;
* Proficient level of English, written \& verbal.


**Problem Solving**
* High competency in data analysis \& critical thinking
* Ability to challenge and engage at all levels of the business
* Able to perform at both a tactical and strategic level in order to report information appropriately in all settings
* Ability to work under pressure and to timescales;
* Ability to recognise and escalate issues in a timely manner;


**Interpersonal Skills**
* Diplomacy skills required in order to work across business boundaries to achieve optimum solutions;
* Exceptional verbal communication skills across different nationalities;
* Presentation skills for effective reporting against areas of responsibility;
* Strong stakeholder management at various levels of authority both internally and externally and confidence to direct challenge/question all levels of the organisation;
* Time Management skills to effectively discharge work across different areas;
* Confidence to hold/chair meetings \& working groups for associated areas of work;
* A self\-starter.

**Job Overview** 




**AX Coin (a member of AXG) is the first and only licensed stablecoin issuer under the regulation of the Central Bank of Bahrain.** 
 We are seeking a Bahrain\-based Director of Risk. This is a senior regulatory leadership role with direct accountability for regulatory integrity, compliance architecture, and legal governance of AX Coin. You will own all regulatory engagement, licensing, compliance frameworks, and enterprise risk management. This role is critical to ensuring AX Coin operates at the highest regulatory standards, with strong, transparent relationships with the Central Bank of Bahrain (CBB) and other regulatory stakeholders.










**Key Responsibilities** 




**1\.Establish and Enhance the Risk Management Framework** 



* Build and continuously refine an Enterprise\-Wide Risk Management Framework (ERMF)commensurate with the size, complexity, and risk profile of the business, covering operational risk, financial risk, compliance risk, technology risk, legal risk, reputational risk, and strategic risk;
* Maintain and update the Risk Register , and conduct regular stress testing and scenario analysis;
* Lead the development and implementation of the Risk Appetite Statement (RAS) , ensuring all business activities remain within acceptable risk tolerance levels.



**2\.Risk Governance and Decision Support** 



* Exercise independent risk review and substantive challenge authority over major business decisions, new project approvals, third\-party outsourcing arrangements, and key partnerships;
* Monitor company\-wide risk exposures and establish a Key Risk Indicator (KRI) system, triggering early warnings and corrective actions when limits are breached;
* Participate in strategic planning and annual budgeting, ensuring business growth targets are feasible within risk capacity.



**3\.Regulatory Engagement and Compliance Reporting** 



* Serve as the company's primary point of contact with the Central Bank of Bahrain (CBB) on all risk management matters, handling regulatory inquiries and examinations;
* Ensure all regulatory submissions (including ICAAP, stress test results, etc., where applicable) are accurate, complete, and timely;
* In accordance with CBB Module FP, ensure that this position continuously satisfies the fit and proper standards of honesty, integrity, financial soundness, and competency, and that all appointment documentation is properly maintained for CBB review.



**4\.Risk Culture and Team Development** 



* Promote a risk\-aware culture throughout the organization through regular training, communication, and performance mechanisms;
* Lead the risk management department, overseeing recruitment, development, and succession planning.



**5\.General Execution** 



* Supervise and execute the day\-to\-day operational execution of the risk function and manage ad\-hoc risk management matters,









**Key Requirements** 




**1\.Education and Professional Qualifications** 



* Bachelor's degree in Risk Management, Finance, Economics, Accounting, Law, or a related field
* Professional certifications such as FRM, PRM, CRM, CRMA, or ISO 31000 are preferred.



**2\.Work Experience** 



* Minimum of 7 years of experience in risk management within a regulated financial institution, FinTech company, or large enterprise, with at least 3 years in a management role;
* Proven track record of establishing and operating an enterprise risk management framework in a financial corporate environment;
* Candidates with legal work experience or a legal background are preferred;
* Hands\-on experience liaising with regulatory authorities (especially the CBB or other GCC regulators) is a strong advantage.



**3\.Core Competencies** 



* In\-depth knowledge of Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) frameworks (e.g., ISO 31000, COSO ERM) and risk governance best practices;
* Familiarity with the CBB regulatory framework and related compliance requirements;
* Strong analytical skills, risk reporting capabilities, and executive\-level communication skills;
* Proven leadership and influencing skills to drive risk culture change in a fast\-paced, high\-growth environment.









**Fit and Proper Requirements (CBB Module FP)** 




 In accordance with the Central Bank of Bahrain's 
 **Fit and Proper Requirements (Module FP)** 
  , candidates for this position are subject to a rigorous fit and proper assessment.
